# algosus architecture

Educational stock trading bot. Two packages in one repo:

- **Frontend:** `src/` — Vite + React dashboard (D3 graph, MUI data grid)
- **Backend:** `functions/src/` — Firebase Cloud Functions (Node 22)

## Trading flow (summary)

1. `scheduleBuy` (Mon 10:00 ET) → OpenAI picks 5 tickers → Alpaca buys → `UpdateProfile` writes to Firebase RTDB
2. `scheduleSell` (Fri 15:50 ET) → Alpaca closes positions → `UpdateProfile` writes to RTDB
3. `getData` HTTP endpoint serves portfolio data to the frontend
4. `src/App.tsx` fetches `getData` on load

## Scripts

- Frontend: `npm run dev`, `npm run build` (repo root)
- Backend: `npm --prefix functions run build`, `serve`, `deploy`, `lint`

## Key entrypoints

- `functions/src/index.ts` — exports all Cloud Functions
- `functions/src/config.ts` — env vars, OpenAI, Alpaca, Firebase init
- `functions/src/buy.ts`, `sell.ts`, `update.ts`, `getData.ts` — core logic
- `src/App.tsx` — frontend data fetch (hardcoded production URL by default)

Read `AGENTS.md` at repo root for the full file map, flow diagram, and git workflow (`main` only).
